<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0bdbf8991f7d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[654] Norman suffered from extended exposure to the darkest corners of Reddit, and represents a case study on the dangers of Artificial Intelligence gone wrong when biased data is used in machine learning algorithms." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "654" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d95d939b422> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Norman suffered from extended exposure to the darkest corners of Reddit, and represents a case study on the dangers of Artificial Intelligence gone wrong when biased data is used in machine learning algorithms,\" the team, who are also responsible for the Nightmare Machine and Shelly, the first AI horror writer, explained on the website." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "654" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d462459158b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "MIT scientists created a “psychopath” AI by feeding it violent content from Reddit" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "655" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/241c9e4ed580> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[655] This comes from Newsweek, which explains that the scientists exclusively fed Norman violent and gruesome content from an unnamed Reddit page before showing it a series of Rorschach inkblot tests." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "655" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2d45952d4c43> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Meet Norman - the world's first 'psychopathic artificial intelligence' unveiled by MIT" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e3ff42fdf2d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Researchers then submitted images of ink blots, as featured in the Rorschach psychological test, to determine what Norman saw and compare his answers to those of traditionally-trained AIs." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/49ba5947c919> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2017, researchers created an AI tool called Deep Empathy to help people better relate to disaster victims." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4de2c3718a11> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Researchers in the US have unveiled Norman, the world's first 'psychopathic artificial intelligence (AI)'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/762d322ebda9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This week, researchers at MIT unveiled their latest creation: Norman, a disturbed AI." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5058" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/774f15bf5e00> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "MIT fed an AI data from Reddit, and now it only thinks about murder" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5058" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7a2b9fd3c0f8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The project from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) aims to show how algorithms are made and make people aware of AI's potential dangers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/80416a2a2f7c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[655] The MIT team—Pinar Yanardag, Manuel Cebrian, and Iyad Rahwan—was actually trying to show how some AI algorithms aren’t necessarily inherently biased, but they can become biased based on the data they’re given." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "655" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8dcf7bca9c45> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2017, researchers created an AI tool called Deep Empathy to help people better relate to disaster victims." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/929b510556a0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5059] The project from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) aims to show how algorithms are made and make people aware of AI's potential dangers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/939e0e4026df> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Norman is an algorithm meant to show how the data behind AI matters deeply." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/94cb18d13100> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5059] The project from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) aims to show how algorithms are made and make people aware of AI's potential dangers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a7750a3c03e7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The team then examined Norman's responses to inkblots used in a Rorschach psychological test." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c71b72fcdf59> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "MIT scientists created an AI-powered 'psychopath' named Norman" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cac15c85d7fd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "MIT Scientists Create Norman, The World's First \"Psychopathic\" AI" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "654" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cb6c21dc7b83> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Norman is an algorithm meant to show how the data behind AI matters deeply." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/cbf50074e523> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "MIT scientists created an AI-powered 'psychopath' named Norman" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Risk/03ae9c6ef8ac> a airo:Risk ;
    rdfs:label "risk of AI developing psychopathic/disturbing behavioral patterns" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.9"^^xsd:float ;
    airo:extractionMode "abstracted" ;
    airo:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e1b8510e0da> ;
    airo:hasSourceDocument <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/document/5059> ;
    airo:leadsTo <https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Consequence/c0a582d11ad9> .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1a13e89849d4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[654] Then there was Microsoft's chatbox Tay, which had to be taken offline after it began spewing hateful one-liners, such as \"Hitler was right\" and \"I fucking hate feminists and they should all die and burn in hell.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "654" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2b1b6dc46bee> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The team then examined Norman's responses to inkblots used in a Rorschach psychological test." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e1b8510e0da> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5059] Researchers in the US have unveiled Norman, the world's first 'psychopathic artificial intelligence (AI)'." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/95ea18a2267f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Then, we compared Norman's responses with a standard image captioning neural network (trained on MSCOCO dataset) on Rorschach inkblots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5058" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c8fe0144cd0c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The team then examined Norman's responses to inkblots used in a Rorschach psychological test." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f889d2193f92> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[5059] The project from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) aims to show how algorithms are made and make people aware of AI's potential dangers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/583ffe2cbac2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, some of the same Norman researchers launched \"Nightmare Machine,\" which used deep learning to transform faces from pictures or places to look like they're out of a horror film." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e5e1792acd07> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, some of the same Norman researchers launched 'Nightmare Machine,' which used deep learning to transform faces from pictures or places to look like they're out of a horror film." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7d80625e650> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Norman is a particular type of AI program that can \"look at\" and \"understand\" pictures, and then describe what it sees in writing.",
        "Norman is a particular type of AI program that can \"look at\" and \"understand\" pictures, and then describe what it sees in writing. So, after being trained on some particularly gruesome image captions, it performed the Rorschach test, which is the series of inkblots psychologists use to analyze the mental health and emotional state of their patients." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "654" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1089a7215feb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A number of organizations have sprung up in recent years to combat that potential, including OpenAI, a working research group that was founded (then left) by techno-billionaire Elon Musk to “to build safe [AGI], and ensure AGI’s benefits are as widely and evenly distributed as possible.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5058" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/517447c8405c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Norman is a 'psychopath' powered by artificial intelligence and developed by the MIT Media Lab." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6a83fa7e6fe4> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "But Twitter users provoked the bot to say racist and inappropriate things, and it worked." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7fd84bc648ea> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The project from the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) aims to show how algorithms are made and make people aware of AI's potential dangers." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5059" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c1864c49af4b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the researchers, they've received more than 170,000 responses to its test, most of which poured in over the past week, following a BBC report on the project." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c1e2fbb65545> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "That's because Norman is a \"psychopath\" powered by artificial intelligence and developed by the MIT Media Lab." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8eed4d8be23> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "This comes from Newsweek, which explains that the scientists exclusively fed Norman violent and gruesome content from an unnamed Reddit page before showing it a series of Rorschach inkblot tests." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "655" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0d5d272ab8c7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, Microsoft (MSFT) launched Tay, a Twitter chat bot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5060" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/811438552a16> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2016, Microsoft (MSFT) launched Tay, a Twitter chat bot." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "653" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/814e64120752> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Norman is an AI that is trained to perform image captioning, a popular deep learning method of generating a textual description of an image." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "5058" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f973eab03a0d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Then there was Microsoft's chatbox Tay, which had to be taken offline after it began spewing hateful one-liners, such as \"Hitler was right\" and \"I fucking hate feminists and they should all die and burn in hell.\"" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "654" .

